# Code owners for this public repository.
#
# Every pull request to the default branch needs an approving review from the
# internal maintainers team. Outside contributors can fork and open PRs, but
# only this team can satisfy the review requirement — and that stays true even
# if someone outside the org is later granted write access, which a plain
# "1 approval" rule would not guarantee.
#
# A team is used rather than individual accounts so that membership changes in
# one place when people join or leave. GitHub silently ignores a code owner
# that has lost write access, so a list of individuals rots without warning.
#
# Requirements for this to work: the team must be visible (not secret) and must
# have write access to this repo. Both are configured.

